WEBVTT

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:13.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday, first of July. All here? Before we start, the charity bake sale on Friday—apparently last year's flapjack is still being talked about.</v>

00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:21.089
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, the charity bake sale on Friday. That flapjack needed a permit to break into. Lovely flavour, mind.</v>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:29.359
<v Grace Liu>Never mind that, whose new car is in the car park? The shiny one taking up about a bay and a half.</v>

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.859
<v Priya Raman>Not mine. Mine's the one where the dirt is doing structural work.</v>

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:40.399
<v Hannah Price>We knew which one you meant before the second sentence.</v>

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:44.200
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, lovely. Actual factory stuff. What's already cleared?</v>

00:00:44.609 --> 00:00:50.909
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah so, already swapped the filter on the gas turbine two yesterday. That's done, not carrying it forward.</v>

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, that's off the outstanding list.</v>

00:00:55.299 --> 00:01:00.549
<v Marcus Hale>And I finished the repair on the line 2 last night. All finished, that one.</v>

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.560
<v Priya Raman>Ah, nice. I saw it running when I came through.</v>

00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:15.060
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Only an observation from me: saw the pressure on the pick and place on two dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:16.459 --> 00:01:18.909
<v Aisha Begum>It recovered without anybody touching it, yeah?</v>

00:01:20.599 --> 00:01:26.549
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, exactly. Just mentioning what I saw, not asking for another job off the back of it.</v>

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:34.150
<v Marcus Hale>Still waiting on parts for the IM1 hydraulic unit, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:39.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, still blocked then. Not something we can move today.</v>

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:47.209
<v Marcus Hale>Same story elsewhere—still waiting on parts for the stretch wrapper, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:50.659
<v Grace Liu>Both sitting on parts, then. No change there.</v>

00:01:51.989 --> 00:01:56.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Let's get the actual jobs straight without mixing those back in.</v>

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.760
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you replace the seals on the Main Water Isolation Valve?</v>

00:02:02.359 --> 00:02:06.209
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll replace the seals on the Main Water Isolation Valve.</v>

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. That's with you.</v>

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.610
<v Grace Liu>Got it. The seals on the Main Water Isolation Valve, not a whole valve replacement.</v>

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:24.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, if you've got a spare minute, can you schedule downtime for the GT2 bearing with production by Thursday?</v>

00:02:26.259 --> 00:02:32.210
<v Marcus Hale>Just getting the downtime agreed with production, yeah? Not saying the bearing work itself is by Thursday?</v>

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:38.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Schedule the downtime by Thursday. If you've got a spare minute—that's where it sits priority-wise.</v>

00:02:40.219 --> 00:02:44.770
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, okay. I'll schedule downtime for the GT2 bearing with production by Thursday.</v>

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.259
<v Marcus Hale>And I'll send the shift handover report round tomorrow at 9:30. That's fairly important.</v>

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:55.930
<v Hannah Price>Tomorrow at 9:30, rather than this morning? Sorry, you clipped out for a second.</v>

00:02:57.849 --> 00:03:00.650
<v Marcus Hale>Tomorrow at 9:30, yeah. I'll send it then.</v>

00:03:01.669 --> 00:03:03.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Marcus. Fairly important, agreed.</v>

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:10.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah Price, can you recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 water valve? Normal priority.</v>

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:19.590
<v Hannah Price>Um, sorry, I can't take that. I haven't got access to the calibration kit, so I need to decline that one.</v>

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:27.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, not with Hannah Price then. Olu, can you take it instead—recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 water valve, normal priority?</v>

00:03:28.639 --> 00:03:34.240
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll take that instead. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 water valve, normal priority.</v>

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.780
<v Priya Raman>That's the sensor calibration we're talking about, not changing the valve setup?</v>

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.419
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, sensor calibration. That's the job I'm taking.</v>

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.629
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve.</v>

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:57.419
<v Aisha Begum>Okay, Sarah. The pressure drop on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve is yours, separate from that calibration.</v>

00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:01.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, separate job. I'll do the investigation.</v>

00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:09.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Marc, can you run a function test on the guard switch on two next week, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:17.230
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll run a function test on the guard switch on two next week, whenever I get a chance.</v>

00:04:18.029 --> 00:04:22.579
<v Grace Liu>Sorry—talked over the end there. Next week, not being squeezed into this shift?</v>

00:04:23.269 --> 00:04:26.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Next week, yeah. Whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:30.959
<v Marcus Hale>That's how I've got it. Next week.</v>

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:42.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah Price, can you go to Tollgate to pick up the replacement parts for the turbine one compressor next Tuesday? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:52.209
<v Hannah Price>Yes, I'll go to Tollgate next Tuesday to pick up the replacement parts for the turbine one compressor. Understood—it matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:59.149
<v Priya Raman>Teams managed to deliver every word of that one. Must like a trip out.</v>

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.980
<v Hannah Price>Unlike me, it doesn't have to sit in the traffic.</v>

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Ha. Right, that's agreed.</v>

00:05:08.689 --> 00:05:12.540
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you run the monthly fire alarm test by Wednesday?</v>

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:22.000
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test by Wednesday. That's today, just so we're both on the same page?</v>

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, today. Wednesday the first.</v>

00:05:27.149 --> 00:05:32.050
<v Grace Liu>First of the month always sneaks up. Feels like we only just had June.</v>

00:05:32.439 --> 00:05:37.689
<v Aisha Begum>Tell me about it. But yes, I've got the monthly fire alarm test by Wednesday.</v>

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:44.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. And neither of those parts-blocked jobs has somehow become live while we've been talking?</v>

00:05:46.829 --> 00:05:53.480
<v Marcus Hale>Nope. IM1 hydraulic unit and stretch wrapper both still waiting. Nothing to do on either until the parts arrive.</v>

00:05:54.389 --> 00:05:59.290
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And my pressure dip was just an observation. No outstanding action attached to that.</v>

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, understood. Kept separate.</v>

00:06:04.569 --> 00:06:09.120
<v Priya Raman>Makes a change having the finished stuff stay finished on the morning call.</v>

00:06:11.399 --> 00:06:14.550
<v Hannah Price>Careful, you'll tempt fate. Back to discussing indestructible flapjack.</v>

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:20.449
<v Marcus Hale>I'm still defending it. Good dunking biscuit, if you've got a big enough mug.</v>

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:27.069
<v Grace Liu>Could use it to mark the parking bays for whoever owns that new car.</v>

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:32.000
<v Sarah Okafor>On that highly technical conclusion, we're done. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:06:33.709 --> 00:06:34.910
<v Aisha Begum>Cheers. Bye.</v>
